    {
      "text": "Let there be no strife, Gen. 13:8. Hatred stirreth up strifes, Prov. 10:12. Only by pride cometh contention, Prov. 13:10. he that is slow to anger appeaseth strife, Prov. 15:18. fool’s lips enter into contention, Prov. 18:6. their contentions are like the bars of a castle, Prov. 18:19. Cast out the scorner, and contention shall go out, Prov. 22:10. who hath contentions, Prov. 23:29. As coals … so is a contentious man to kindle strife, Prov. 26:21.",
